<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tokharistan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tukharistan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tokharistan was the medieval name for former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a>, the lands on both sides of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a> and Tajikistan. It was ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hephthalites">Hephthalites</a> and then, from the 7th century, by Turkic yabghus under Western Turkic overlordship, before falling to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> in the 8th century. Its cities included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkh">Balkh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/termez">Termez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kunduz">Kunduz</a>.</p></div>
